The paper confirms that the native search problem is exact binary syndrome decoding: find a weight-\(t\) error \(e\) with \(He^\top=s^\top\). It also explicitly warns that decoding becomes polynomial in a broad high-weight regime, while the Gilbert–Varshamov regime has roughly one solution and all cited generic decoders remain exponential. I’m now checking whether a planted random full-rank matrix really stays in that regime and whether the required standard decoding attack can be measured honestly.
