codex
Implemented a native Track A syndrome-decoding generator based on the paper’s Problem 1.1 and Gilbert–Varshamov regime ([paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2208.02201v3)).

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/gen_2208_02201.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass. Highlights: 0/200,000 legal guesses, four attacks at 0/8, exact demo count 1/66, and a median 5,158,992 XOR operations for the capped Prange baseline.

The result is not submission-ready because OpenRouter returned account-level HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for every vendor and retry. The transcripts preserve those errors but do not claim model failures or a hardened verdict. A refreshed OpenRouter key is required to rerun the three oracle arms.
