Both figures correspond to parity-checks $\hv_{\sN}$ of weight $6$ and to $s=19$. However they differ in the value for $k$.
$k$ equals $26$ in the first figure and displays rather heavy tails for the largest Fourier coefficients corresponding to the parity-checks $\hv_{\sN}$ whereas $k=40$ corresponds to rather similar tails
