codex
The oracle script is externally blocked: all four redraws returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” and the harness correctly refused to score those as model failures. I’m preserving that script-owned evidence, not fabricating a verdict. The generator and local reports remain usable, but the README will continue to mark submission/hardening as pending until a funded key can complete the three oracle arms.
The native Track A generator is implemented and all local gates pass. The required oracle stage was attempted but OpenRouter rejected every redraw because the configured key's total limit is exhausted; this is an external blocker, not a family rejection.
  ✓ Read the full paper and perform G/H/V plus Track A/B triage
  ✓ Inspect repository harness and implement the generator if viable
  ✓ Run self-tests, adversary attacks, and repair failures
  • Run the required bare and G9 oracle loops if credentials permit
  → Write final reports and verify all deliverables
