codex
Built and locally verified the Track A syndrome-decoding generator from [arXiv:2208.02201](https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.02201).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2208_02201.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/gen_2208_02201.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local gates all pass, including 0/200,000 legal random guesses, four attacks at 0/8 successes, and 40/40 relabelling checks. Paper references were corrected to Assumption 3.7, Conjecture 3.11, and Propositions 4.4/5.1.

The sole blocker is STEP 4: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” on every redraw, leaving zero scored oracle attempts. The error transcripts are preserved honestly; the family is not rejected, but it must not be submitted as hardened until rerun with a funded `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`.
