codex
Implemented a native Track B LPN problem generator based on [arXiv:2208.02201](https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.02201).

Key results:

- All local gates G1–G9(c) pass.
- Exact solution count: 1.
- Guess probability: \(4.768\times10^{-7}\); 0/200,000 sampled hits.
- Four attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Paper’s Walsh–Hadamard algorithm: 48,234,493 measured operations.
- Compact structural route: verified in 60 XORs.
- Answer size: at most 54 characters / approximately 14 tokens.

Deliverables:

- [gen_2208_02201.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/gen_2208_02201.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2208.02201/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The only remaining blocker is external: every oracle call returned OpenRouter HTTP 403, “Key limit exceeded.” The transcripts preserve those errors, but no oracle-hardness verdict is claimed, and the result should not be submitted until rerun with a working `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`.
